{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_22-30-45-hashicorp_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Apply admission reaches the leader main loop, which assigns term/index and stores logs before reporting self support. Per-peer replication sends bounded batches with previous index/term, retries rejected prefixes and falls back to snapshots for missing history. Follower append persists nonduplicate entries before success. The leader-lifetime commitment tracker counts only current voters, advances at a majority index only after the first entry of this term is supported, and notifies the main loop. That loop advances commit/configuration state and enqueues committed tuples for runFSM; FSM application supplies command responses. Replication CommitTimeout carries the leader commit frontier to idle followers; their processLogs path feeds the same serialized FSM consumer.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-dispatch\",\n        \"B-replicate\",\n        \"B-commitment\",\n        \"B-leader-consume\",\n        \"B-append\",\n        \"B-fsm\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-match\",\n        \"F-commit-frontier\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-dispatch\",\n        \"s-replication\",\n        \"s-commitment\",\n        \"s-leader-loop\",\n        \"s-append\",\n        \"s-fsm\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A follower without recent contact campaigns only if it is a voter. Per-attempt pre-vote/election channels isolate replies; real elections persist term and vote, and remote handlers enforce term, candidate eligibility, prior vote and log freshness. A winning majority creates a fresh leader commitment/replication lifetime and appends a current-term noop. Newer-term RPCs, replication rejection signals, voter-only lease loss or committed local removal can end leadership. Cleanup stops old workers and rejects pending futures; surviving old replies refer to old tracker/channel objects. Already enqueued FSM work has its own owner and may complete after stepdown. Persistent logs/snapshots and vote freshness carry prior decided history into later campaigns; new leaders collect fresh replication support.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-election\",\n        \"B-leader-lifetime\",\n        \"B-lease\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-match\",\n        \"F-commit-frontier\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-follower\",\n        \"s-candidate\",\n        \"s-election\",\n        \"s-vote\",\n        \"s-leader-setup\",\n        \"s-lease\",\n        \"s-recovery\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"The authority context selects both the log that may be advanced and the eligible voters whose support can advance it. Membership is logged, normally one uncommitted change at a time, and updates the commitment voter set and replication workers immediately; followers roll back latest membership with a conflicting suffix. Elections compare retained log/snapshot history, while the current-term commitment threshold prevents using mere old-term support as fresh authority. Recovery reconstructs history and configuration before campaigning. Heartbeats confirm contact but carry no commit index; VerifyLeader consumes separate per-request callbacks and lease checks count recent voter contacts. Verification registration includes nonvoter replication workers despite a voter-derived threshold, retained as an unresolved eligibility question rather than a guarantee.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-configuration\",\n        \"B-leader-lifetime\",\n        \"B-recovery\",\n        \"B-verify-admit\",\n        \"B-verify-notify\",\n        \"B-verify-complete\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-match\",\n        \"F-commit-frontier\",\n        \"F-verify-tally\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-config-append\",\n        \"s-repl-membership\",\n        \"s-commitment\",\n        \"s-append\",\n        \"s-recovery\",\n        \"s-verify-register\",\n        \"s-verify-future\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Verification acknowledgment eligibility with nonvoters and independent lease timing.\",\n      \"Follower commit bound versus request-checked prefix under recovery/backtracking histories.\",\n      \"Storage failures between separate vote-key updates; pipeline error and peer-address transition details.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation and context lifecycles, their producers/consumers and necessary membership/recovery/completion paths are traced. Usable navigation does not mean exhaustive coverage or correctness.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"2124e49b338f4dd49a39bd8567e44b76\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"2124e49b338f4dd49a39bd8567e44b76\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dedf7b309d374d558784f5abb2cc004a\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n        \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"controlled_schedule\",\n        \"question\": \"Can VerifyLeader consume affirmative acknowledgments from Nonvoter replication workers as the voter majority needed to confirm current leadership, and can that produce successful verification without eligible authority support under a legal history?\",\n        \"importance\": \"A false positive in the documented stale-read protection can expose stale FSM state after a voter majority has moved to another leader; local acknowledgment eligibility is the first discriminator, not yet an observed cluster consequence.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"s-append\",\n          \"s-candidate\",\n          \"s-config-append\",\n          \"s-config-change\",\n          \"s-config-contract\",\n          \"s-election\",\n          \"s-follower\",\n          \"s-heartbeat\",\n          \"s-install\",\n          \"s-leader-loop\",\n          \"s-lease\",\n          \"s-recovery\",\n          \"s-repl-membership\",\n          \"s-repl-notify\",\n          \"s-repl-result\",\n          \"s-repl-snapshot\",\n          \"s-verify-api\",\n          \"s-verify-future\